maria: FYI I opened a docs PR (3299) to unify the streaming pagination snippets across py/ts/go. Main ask: clarify the resume cursor name (we currently show `resume_token`, `resumeToken`, and `cursor` in different examples) and add a tiny checkpointing example for long-running consumers.

li: thanks — link? will grab a quick look.

maria: https://github.com/redwood-inference/docs/pull/3299 — preview failing only because the TS snippet errors in the sandbox (type mismatch). CI otherwise green.

ryan: I can take TS. Is the plan to standardize on the docs name only, or to propose an API alias as well?

maria: Prefer keeping SDK surface stable, but docs should normalize the concept and show the mapping: Python `resume_token`, TS `resumeToken`, Go `ResumeCursor`. Add a short note that the field name differs between languages but semantics are identical.

sam: I'll add a Go snippet showing a resume loop using a channel to process items without buffering. Also will show how to persist the cursor to a DB after each completed page.

li: here's a Python generator sketch for checkpointing: 

```py
async def items_with_checkpoint(client, start_token=None, persist_fn=None):
    token = start_token
    while True:
        page = await client.streaming.list_items(page_cursor=token)
        async for it in page:
            yield it
        # commit checkpoint once page fully emitted
        token = getattr(page, "resume_token", None)
        if token and persist_fn:
            await persist_fn(token)
        if not token:
            break
```

note: emphasize persisting only after the page completes to avoid duplicate work on resume.

ryan: TS fix: the sandbox complained because our sample used `for await (const p of client.streaming.listPages())` but then assumed `p.resumeToken` exists while the iterator yields chunk objects. Updated snippet to access resume token from the page wrapper the SDK exposes. I'll push a minimal example: 

```ts
for await (const page of client.streaming.listPages({ pageCursor: startCursor })) {
  for (const item of page.items) {
    handle(item)
  }
  // page.resumeToken is set after page emission
  startCursor = (page as any).resumeToken ?? null
  if (startCursor) await db.saveCursor(startCursor)
}
```

sam: Go snippet (concept): 

```go
for {
  resp := client.Streaming.ListItems(ctx, &ListReq{PageCursor: cursor})
  ch := make(chan Item)
  go func() {
    for resp.Scan() {
      ch <- resp.Item()
    }
    close(ch)
  }()
  for it := range ch {
    process(it)
  }
  cursor = resp.ResumeCursor()
  if cursor == "" { break }
  db.SaveCursor(cursor)
}
```

maria: Perfect. Two doc nits: 1) add a short paragraph on retry semantics: "Do not retry single items mid-page; restart the stream from the last persisted resume cursor to guarantee idempotency." 2) add cross-link to SDK reference for the language-specific field names.

li: I'll update the TS sample to avoid `any` cast by referencing the typed `Page` interface. Also adding a one-line note about backpressure: prefer small page sizes when latency-sensitive.

